Files derived from that work, and what changed:

  plugins/shunt/scripts/bulk-read         unchanged but for the library it sources
                                          and its token-usage line
  plugins/shunt/scripts/code-write        unchanged but for the library it sources
                                          and its token-usage line
  plugins/shunt/scripts/shunt-stats       new in this fork: summarizes the savings
                                          ledger — per harness, per triggering
                                          function, per worker and mode, plus the
                                          gate blocks that never became delegations
  install.sh                             new in this fork: installs into Claude
                                          Code, Codex CLI, Gemini CLI and DeepSeek
                                          Harness, pins per-host workers, and can
                                          compose DSH's dsh-hooks-claude-code
                                          bridge for the hard read gate
  plugins/shunt/scripts/lib/worker.sh     rewritten from scripts/lib/aika.sh: the
                                          Spotify Portal / AiKA transport is replaced
                                          by one headless turn on claude, gemini or
                                          codex, chosen at run time; the turn runs
                                          under a timeout resolved at call time (GNU
                                          timeout, gtimeout, or a perl watchdog),
                                          so macOS needs no coreutils; the claude
                                          turn pins --setting-sources project and
                                          --strict-mcp-config, because the empty
                                          scope string is invalid and falls back to
                                          loading the account's plugins and its
                                          claude.ai connector MCP tool schemas;
                                          every delegation is recorded in a JSONL
                                          savings ledger (SHUNT_STATS_FILE) with a
                                          kind (delegation) and, when passed, the
                                          --via triggering function, under host dsh
                                          when DSH_SESSION_ID/DSH_SHELL say the
                                          call came from DeepSeek Harness
  plugins/shunt/hooks/check-file-size     blocks with exit 2 + stderr instead of a
                                          decision envelope, so Codex and Gemini CLI
                                          honour it too; handles batch reads and the
                                          absolute_path argument; names a runnable
                                          command in the refusal; the refusal tags
                                          --via read-gate and the block is recorded
                                          as a gate event in the savings ledger
  plugins/shunt/hooks/check-bash-read     same refusal change, plus it unwraps a
                                          `bash -lc "…"` layer and an argv array;
                                          a transparent `rtk proxy ` prefix is
                                          unwrapped and `rtk read` is read as
                                          cat, so an rtk-instructed agent cannot
                                          slip a big read past the gate; the refusal
                                          tags --via bash-gate and the block is
                                          recorded as a gate event
  plugins/shunt/hooks/hooks.json          matcher widened for Codex tool names
  plugins/shunt/skills/*/SKILL.md         reworded: worker model, not AiKA
  plugins/shunt/evals/*                   decisions asserted by exit code; transport
                                          evals stub the three CLIs on PATH; 13 cases
                                          added for the new input shapes; the codex-
                                          noise check no longer embeds a case
                                          statement in $( ), which macOS bash 3.2
                                          cannot parse; a failed benchmark delegation
                                          is reported as a failed row, never as a
                                          0-token answer; the ledger is redirected
                                          to a temp file and its records asserted
